            <ArticleTitle>Dorsal defect of the patella: MR features.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>474-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dorsal defect of the patella (DDP) is a benign lesion with characteristic radiologic features. We describe the MR appearance of a typical DDP and a healed DDP as seen in two patients. The classic CT appearance is also described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
